phi-transport-api (1.2.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Interface break: the data path is UTF-8 JSON text. topic, payloads, config and
    SyncResult::payloadJson are text instead of QString/QJsonObject, so core can
    serialize an event once for all transports and a transport can forward it to its
    wire without parsing. Qt leaves the data path; identity strings and the
    diagnostics types (LogEntry, Error) still use it.
  * Add the Qt-free jsontext.h with the envelope assembly helpers (jsonQuoted,
    jsonField, withJsonField) and a ctest target covering them - escaping, control
    characters, UTF-8 pass-through and the splice cases that would otherwise put a
    malformed frame on the wire (part of F-41).
  * invokeAsync takes the plugin type as a parameter; it used to travel as a
    __phiTransportPluginType key inside the caller's payload (F-40).
  * IID is now .../TransportInterface/1.2 and kTransportApiVersion is 1.2.0.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:51:13 +0200

phi-transport-api (1.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * static_assert the shared log numbering (LogLevel, LogCategory ranges) and state
    in PROTOCOLL.md that it is shared with the adapter plane and the wire, so the
    two cannot drift apart again (F-39).

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:30:02 +0200

phi-transport-api (1.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Interface break within the v1 line: TransportInterface is stateless and the
    core facade plus the log/call helpers moved to the new header-only
    TransportPluginBase. Transports derive from the base and drop their
    apiVersion() override.
  * Plugin IID is now .../TransportInterface/1.1 and kTransportApiVersion is
    added: phi-core refuses a transport built against another interface version at
    load instead of binding it to a mismatched vtable (F-38). The IID changes even
    though the version stays in the v1 line, because the guard has to be able to
    tell the two builds apart.
  * Version the package by the API version instead of a git snapshot, so
    consumers can express phi-transport-api-dev (>= 1.1.0) as a package relation.
  * Documented that this is a source API with no binary compatibility, and that
    adapters (southbound) and transports (northbound) are told apart by direction
    rather than by protocol name.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:23:17 +0200

